=== PARITY (web source reproduced end-to-end) ===
  Web AdvancedSettings.tsx is the "Restore confirmation prompts" panel: it reads
  listSilenced() from lib/confirmSilence.ts (localStorage `teslasync:confirm-silence:v1`,
  a deduped+sorted string array) and bumps a local `tick` after each unsilence /
  clearAllSilenced so it re-reads. useSilenceKeyLabel maps known ids to friendly labels
  (discard-draft, unsaved-navigation) and falls back to the raw key for forward-compat.
  - Data sources (web useSilenceKeyLabel + useTranslation): bound through the P1/S8 seam
    AdvancedSettingsStore → AdvancedSettingsModel; no I/O in the view. The native
    UserDefaultsConfirmSilenceStore reads/writes the EXACT web `STORAGE_KEY`
    (`teslasync:confirm-silence:v1`) as a JSON string array, deduped + sorted, with a
    missing/corrupt payload reading empty (web load() defensive catch).
  - Composition (web GlassPanel + IconBox + Button + EmptyState + FadeIn):
      • FadeIn delay={0.24}  -> TSFadeIn(delay: 0.24).
      • GlassPanel           -> TSGlassPanel.
      • IconBox color="cyan" -> TSIconBox(tone: .info) (cyan token) + question glyph.
      • header               -> title (.isHeader) + muted description + (when rows>0)
                                "Restore all" ghost TSButton with the RotateCcw → SF
                                "arrow.counterclockwise" glyph (web silenced.length > 0 gate).
      • EmptyState           -> AdvancedSettingsEmptyView (ContentUnavailableView) carrying
                                the web "tick Don't ask again to silence" hint.
      • <ul divide-y border> -> SilencedPromptList: bordered, hairline-divided rows; each
                                row = labelFor(key) (single-line truncated, web `truncate`)
                                + per-row "Restore" ghost TSButton (web RotateCcw).
  - States (ALL rendered — each a #if DEBUG preview + a projection/model unit test):
      loading (initial read → skeleton chrome) · empty (web silenced.length === 0 →
      friendly state, never a blank box) · content (sorted restore rows) · error (read
      failure → Retry, standard P4 envelope) · stale (freshness chip + "Reconnecting"
      banner + one-shot auto-refresh on the transition) · offline (cached rows + "Offline"
      chip/banner). The web source has only empty/content; loading/error/stale/offline are
      the prompt-mandated P4 envelope, reachable via the store seam (exercised by previews
      + tests). The UserDefaults store mirrors web (always live; corrupt→empty).
  - i18n (P1/S10): web keys preserved — advanced.restoreConfirms.title / .description /
    .restoreAll / .restore / .empty, and the useSilenceKeyLabel labels
    advanced.restoreConfirms.keys.discardDraft / .keys.unsavedNavigation; native chrome
    namespaced advanced.restoreConfirms.* (loading/emptyTitle/errorTitle/retry/promptRole/
    live/stale/offline/staleBanner/offlineBanner/a11y.*). All 22 code-referenced keys are
    declared in AdvancedSettings.strings (referenced⊆declared verified, diff empty); NO
    English string literals in native code (all via AdvancedSettingsStrings + Text(verbatim:)).
  - Accessibility: VoiceOver labels on the panel; the header carries .isHeader; each row's
    "Restore" button names its prompt ("Restore “<label>”"); the list carries a combined
    "%d silenced prompts" summary; the freshness chip + Retry are labelled; Dynamic-Type
    system fonts (Font.TS); reduce-motion honored (TSFadeIn; static skeleton).
  - Telemetry (P1/S11): AdvancedSettingsModel.start() emits view.opened with surface slug
    "AdvancedSettings" exactly once (OSLogAdvancedSettingsTelemetry default; prod app injects
    the shared diagnostics adapter). Asserted by testStartEmitsViewOpenedOnceAndStartsStore.

